---
# Exception-specification hygiene only. This is not a general lint profile.
#
#   bugprone-exception-escape  a noexcept function (or destructor / move
#                              operation) that can reach a throw. In this
#                              project it also surfaces hot-path functions that
#                              call into containers which can grow.
#   performance-noexcept-*     move constructors, swap and destructors that
#                              should be noexcept and are not.
#
# bugprone-exception-escape switches itself off in a translation unit compiled
# with -fno-exceptions, which is how the hot modules are built, so it reports
# nothing there by default. scripts/run_tidy.py adds -fexceptions for the
# analysis; run tidy through it rather than directly.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-exception-escape,
  performance-noexcept-move-constructor,
  performance-noexcept-swap,
  performance-noexcept-destructor
